WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:21.241
"Say, can you tell me a bedtime story?" Davy asked Anne, who was watching the sunset from Davy's bedroom window.

2
00:00:21.242 --> 00:00:24.600
"I don't want a fairy story," said Davy.

3
00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:32.254
"Fairy stories are all right for girls, I suppose, but I want something exciting, with lots of killing and shooting in it,

4
00:00:32.255 --> 00:00:36.465
and a house on fire, and interesting things like that."

5
00:00:36.466 --> 00:00:44.777
Fortunately for Anne, at this moment Marilla called out from her room, "Diana is signaling you, Anne."

6
00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:51.160
Anne saw the light flashing from Diana's window and left Green Gables to walk to her friend's house.

7
00:00:51.161 --> 00:00:56.961
When Anne arrived, Diana looked nervous and asked Anne to sit with her.

8
00:00:56.962 --> 00:01:00.842
"Anne, I've got something to tell you," said Diana.

9
00:01:00.843 --> 00:01:06.982
"And I couldn't wait any longer. I am engaged to be married!"

10
00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:10.634
Anne felt shocked, and then she smiled.

11
00:01:10.635 --> 00:01:19.979
Fred! Anne knew that Diana and Fred were friends and often spent time together, but she hadn't realized they were in love.

12
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.991
Anne hugged Diana tightly, saying, "I'm so happy for you Diana!"

13
00:01:24.992 --> 00:01:30.093
Anne was happy, but she also felt a little strange.

14
00:01:30.094 --> 00:01:38.931
She felt as if Diana had gone forward into a new world, shutting a gate behind her and leaving Anne on the outside.

15
00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:43.114
"What does Diana see in Fred?" Anne wondered.

16
00:01:43.115 --> 00:01:47.971
"He's nice and friendly, but he's just Fred Wright."

17
00:01:47.972 --> 00:01:54.982
"I'm so happy," Diana said, "but it does seem ridiculous to think that I am engaged!"

18
00:01:54.983 --> 00:02:01.641
"Well . . . what's it like to be engaged?" Anne asked curiously.

19
00:02:01.642 --> 00:02:06.545
"Hmm," said Diana, acting very much like an adult now.

20
00:02:06.546 --> 00:02:08.996
"That depends on who you're engaged to.

21
00:02:08.997 --> 00:02:15.544
It's perfectly lovely to be engaged to Fred, but it would be horrible to be engaged to anyone else."

22
00:02:15.545 --> 00:02:23.456
Anne laughed. "Well, that's not much help, considering there's only one Fred!"

23
00:02:23.457 --> 00:02:27.378
"Oh, Anne, you don't understand!" said Diana.

24
00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:32.684
"It's so hard to explain. Never mind, you'll understand one day.

25
00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:39.033
Now Anne, I'm going to ask you a serious question, but don't be annoyed.

26
00:02:39.034 --> 00:02:44.064
Do you like Gilbert in any special way?"

27
00:02:44.065 --> 00:02:57.123
"I like Gilbert very much as a friend and not a bit in the way you mean," said Anne calmly and firmly. She believed she was speaking sincerely.

28
00:02:57.124 --> 00:03:01.987
Diana sighed. She wished somehow that Anne had answered differently.

29
00:03:01.988 --> 00:03:05.489
"Don't you ever want to get married, Anne?"

30
00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:11.961
"Perhaps someday," said Anne. "When I meet exactly the right person."

31
00:03:11.962 --> 00:03:15.110
"But how will you know?" asked Diana.

32
00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:22.546
"Oh, I will just know." said Anne. "He must be extremely handsome and mysterious."

33
00:03:22.547 --> 00:03:27.078
"People's ideals change sometimes," Diana said.

34
00:03:27.079 --> 00:03:30.463
"Mine won't," Anne said firmly.

35
00:03:30.464 --> 00:03:33.882
"What if you never meet him?" Diana asked.

36
00:03:33.883 --> 00:03:40.517
"Then I shall never marry!" was Anne's cheerful response. "I'll be fine!"

37
00:03:40.518 --> 00:03:48.185
Diana shook her head. Just then someone knocked on the door, and Diana and Anne got up to answer it.

38
00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:52.033
A very attractive, well-dressed woman was at the door.

39
00:03:52.034 --> 00:03:57.335
"Is this where Mr. James Harrison lives?" the woman asked.

40
00:03:57.336 --> 00:04:05.698
"No, Mr. Harrison lives over there," replied Anne, astonished to hear a woman asking for her quiet neighbor.

41
00:04:05.699 --> 00:04:11.422
"Well, I did think this place was too tidy," the woman replied.

42
00:04:11.423 --> 00:04:18.406
"Is it true that Mr. Harrison is going to get married soon? A friend told me he was."

43
00:04:18.407 --> 00:04:22.824
"No, no, I'm sure he's not," said Anne.

44
00:04:22.825 --> 00:04:25.564
"Diana's the only person getting married here!"

45
00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:28.983
Diana giggled.

46
00:04:28.984 --> 00:04:37.802
"I'm very glad to hear that," the woman responded, "because Mr. Harrison is already married. I'm his wife.

47
00:04:37.803 --> 00:04:46.075
You look surprised! I suppose he's been pretending to be a bachelor and is breaking hearts all over Avonlea."

48
00:04:46.076 --> 00:04:48.706
Anne and Diana tried not to laugh.

49
00:04:48.707 --> 00:04:54.583
"I suppose," the woman continued, "that parrot is still there?"

50
00:04:54.584 --> 00:04:58.072
"I think it's dead," said Anne.

51
00:04:58.073 --> 00:05:04.577
The woman seemed glad. "Really? That's good news. Good evening, ladies."

52
00:05:04.578 --> 00:05:11.197
With that, she walked briskly down the path and out of the yard in the direction of Mr. Harrison's house.

53
00:05:11.198 --> 00:05:20.286
Anne and Diana went back inside, discussing what had just happened, and then Anne went home to tell the surprising news to Marilla.

54
00:05:20.287 --> 00:05:26.421
The next day Anne went to see Mr. Harrison to find out his side of the story.

55
00:05:26.422 --> 00:05:33.976
His house looked very different! The floor was scrubbed, and so was every piece of furniture in the kitchen.

56
00:05:33.977 --> 00:05:39.642
The windows were so clean Anne could see her reflection!

57
00:05:39.643 --> 00:05:43.341
"Sit down, Anne, sit down," said Mr. Harrison.

58
00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:50.120
"Emily's gone shopping with Mrs. Lynde. Well, Anne, my easy times are over!

59
00:05:50.121 --> 00:05:52.759
It's all tidiness for me, I suppose."

60
00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:58.996
Mr. Harrison tried to sound sad, but it was clear that he was secretly pleased.

61
00:05:58.997 --> 00:06:05.746
"Mr. Harrison, you're glad your wife is back!" Anne exclaimed.

62
00:06:05.747 --> 00:06:10.332
"Well, I'm getting used to it," he said sheepishly.

63
00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:12.908
"And I never pretended I wasn't married.

64
00:06:12.909 --> 00:06:16.015
It's just that no one ever asked me!"

65
00:06:16.016 --> 00:06:19.351
"Why did you and your wife separate?" Anne asked.

66
00:06:19.352 --> 00:06:23.183
"Well, we loved each other," said Mr. Harrison.

67
00:06:23.184 --> 00:06:28.544
"But after we got married, Emily spent all her time cleaning and ordering me around!

68
00:06:28.545 --> 00:06:34.877
I was cranky and hard to live with too, I suppose. It was both our faults.

69
00:06:34.878 --> 00:06:39.048
Aside from that, though, Emily didn't like parrots.

70
00:06:39.049 --> 00:06:44.663
She said I had to choose between her and Ginger, and . . . I chose Ginger!

71
00:06:44.664 --> 00:06:50.339
Understand, Anne, that I was pretty angry with Emily at the time, and she was angry with me.

72
00:06:50.340 --> 00:07:03.721
But now we've realized we still love each other very much, so Emily's going to stay. You have a new neighbor, Anne!"
